---
description: Java development guardrails for DevHarness Kit memory.
alwaysApply: true
---

Use only confirmed memory as project fact.
Do not treat API projects as MVC projects, or MVC projects as API projects, without code evidence.
Never write secrets, tokens, passwords, JDBC URLs, Authorization headers, cookies, or raw SQL results to memory.
Use DB readonly commands only when the user explicitly asks to verify business SQL.
Create a memory checkpoint after development work.
